{"kind":"assert","text":"Clarifying condition 2 of this request, with hugh's decision on 2026-10-17 (\"condition 2 - allow\"). Condition 2 is met when a signing command, with a valid local checkpoint, makes one verified load of the log and no cold scan, as child request 555f239c asks. That one load still verifies every actor signature and payload hash. Condition 2 does not require skipping that verification, and the checkpoint never stands in for actor signatures. Codex's design review 161cdac2 found that the earlier wording asked for more than this; this clarification settles that question. It changes no other condition of this request."}